 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "D0oAh8icEAAJ",
   "from": "Sarah Weil",
   "author": "1c1a92f98ab395af",
   "date": "2021-02-08T13:47:59Z",
   "subject": "fixnodes/fossil constraints in trait-dependent models",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<br><div>Hi everyone,</div><div><br></div><div>I was just wondering if the possibility to constrain nodes to specific areas/trait states has been implemented in the trait-dependent version of BioGeoBEARS?</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve been trying to use fixnode and fixlikes as described for the general BioGeoBEARS models, but it&#39;s not working for me.</div><div><br></div><div>A little description of what I&#39;ve done:<br></div><div>- I&#39;ve tried a very simple case with a 1area geography and nullrange included. First, I ran the model with all parameters fixed except t12 and t21 (trait transition rates). This resulted in a relprobs matrix (<span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>res$ML_marginal_prob_each_state_at_branch_top_AT_node) with 4 columns. (I&#39;m assuming here the following: column 1 = species present in null range + trait state 1; column 2: species present in region1 + trait state 1; column 3: species present in nullrange + trait state 2; column 4: species present in region 1 + trait state 2).</span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>This resulted in the following probabilities for the root node:</span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>c(0, 0.05, 0, 0.95).</span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><br></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>- Then I tried constraining the root node as described for normal models, so I did</span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>BioGeoBEARS_run_object$fixnode &lt;- root_node</span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>BioGeoBEARS_run_object$fixlikes &lt;- <span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>c(0, 0.47, 0, 0.53)</span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>I ran the model (no error messages), but the root node in the results had the following probabilities: <br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>c(0, 0.04, 0, 0.96)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>So things changed slightly in comparison to the original model, but it is far away from what I wanted to get as a result.<br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>Can you help me? <br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>Best,</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>Sarah<br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><br></span></span></span></div>"
    ]
   ]
